items.summary:
When a user-designated `framework.md` or similarly named framework file is described as the analysis baseline, treat it as the estimand/method/guardrail contract, not as a live current-result report.

Do not call the framework "wrong" merely because current result artifacts, counts, paths, or checkpoints have advanced beyond examples or planning notes inside the framework. Instead:

- judge current analyses and reports against the framework-defined estimand, correction rules, evidence boundaries, and interpretation redlines;
- update result/report artifacts when outputs change;
- edit the framework only when the analysis contract itself changes or the user explicitly asks to revise it.
